---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How DPEEN collects, uses and protects personal information when you visit our website or contact us."
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what personal information the Drug Prevention Education
    and Empowerment Network (“DPEEN”, “we”, “us”) collects through
    dpeenetwork.com, why we collect it, and the choices you have. We keep it
    short because we collect very little.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    DPEEN is the organisation responsible for the personal information described
    here. You can reach us at{' '}
    <a href="mailto:info@dpeenetwork.com">info@dpeenetwork.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Enquiry forms.</strong> When you write to us through the site we
      receive your full name, email address, the reason you are getting in
      touch, and any message you choose to add. Please do not include sensitive
      details such as health information unless you want to share them with us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Technical data.</strong> Our hosting provider automatically
      records standard server information, such as your IP address, browser
      type, the pages requested and the time of the request. We use it to keep
      the site secure and working, not to build a profile of you.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Donations.</strong> Donations are made by bank transfer from your
      own banking app. We do not take card payments on this site, and the site
      never sees your bank login or card details.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not ask you to create an account, and we do not run advertising or
    analytics tools on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>3. How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To reply to your message and follow up on your enquiry.</li>
    <li>
      To arrange volunteering, partnerships or help requests you ask us about.
    </li>
    <li>
      To keep the website secure and prevent spam or misuse, for example with a
      hidden spam-trap field and checks on where form submissions come from.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell your information, we do not send marketing emails unless you
    ask for them, and we do not make automated decisions about you.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Why we are allowed to use it</h2>
  <p>
    We use the information you send because you asked us to respond, and because
    we have a legitimate interest in running our programmes and protecting our
    website. Where the law requires your consent, we rely on it, and you may
    withdraw it at any time.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    Only people at DPEEN who need to handle your enquiry can see it. We use the
    following service providers to run the site, and they process information on
    our behalf:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Vercel</strong>, which hosts the website and its contact form.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Purelymail</strong>, which delivers and stores the email we
      receive.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Fonts</strong> and <strong>Unsplash</strong>, which supply
      the typeface and some photographs. Your browser contacts them directly
      when a page loads, so they receive your IP address and browser details.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We may also disclose information when the law requires it or to protect
    people from harm.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Transfers outside your country</h2>
  <p>
    Some of these providers operate servers outside Nigeria, including in the
    United States. By using the site and contacting us you understand that your
    information may be processed there, subject to the safeguards each provider
    applies.
  </p>

  <h2>7. How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep enquiries only for as long as we need them to deal with your request
    and to keep reasonable records of our work. You can ask us to delete your
    message at any time, and we will do so unless the law requires us to keep
    it.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Security</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served over HTTPS, and we take reasonable steps to protect the
    information we hold. No online service can be completely secure, so please
    take care with what you send.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 and similar laws, you may ask us
    to give you a copy of your information, correct it, delete it, restrict or
    object to how we use it, or move it elsewhere. You may also withdraw consent
    you have given. Email{' '}
    <a href="mailto:info@dpeenetwork.com">info@dpeenetwork.com</a> and we will
    respond as soon as we reasonably can. If you are unhappy with our response,
    you may complain to the Nigeria Data Protection Commission or to the data
    protection authority where you live.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Children</h2>
  <p>
    Our programmes support young people, but this website is aimed at adults. If
    you are under 18, please ask a parent or guardian to contact us for you.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Other websites</h2>
  <p>
    If we link to another website, its owner is responsible for how it handles
    your information, so please read their policy.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We will post any changes on this page and update the date at the top. For
    how we use cookies and similar storage, see our{' '}
    <a href="/cookies/">cookie policy</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
